  "lineage": "Late-1980s-and-onward Southern US hip-hop tradition spanning Houston (Geto Boys, Rap-A-Lot Records), Atlanta (Outkast, Dungeon Family), Miami (2 Live Crew, Miami Bass), and Memphis (Three 6 Mafia). Characterized by drawled vocal-delivery, Roland 808-prominent production, and explicit Southern-cultural-identity assertion against the East Coast / West Coast geographic dichotomy. Outkast's Aquemini (1998) and Geto Boys' We Can't Be Stopped (1991) consolidated regional visibility.",
